TITLE:: PianoRoll
SUMMARY:: Piano-roll view for MIDI recording and note editing.
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events
RELATED:: Classes/PianoRollContainer, Classes/PianoRollNote, Classes/PianoRollSidebar, Classes/PianoRollTimeline, Classes/PianoRollLoopMarkers, Classes/SequencePlayer, Classes/Sequencer, Classes/SequencerGui, Classes/SequencerDocument, Classes/Metronome, Classes/SequencerKeyRouter, Classes/AmpCommand, Classes/DeleteCommand, Classes/LeftCommand, Classes/LegatoCommand, Classes/RightCommand, Classes/SnapCommand, Classes/TransposeCommand, Classes/WriteCommand

DESCRIPTION::
LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: is a LINK::Classes/SCViewHolder:: that shows recorded notes as a piano roll. Its root LINK::Classes/View:: uses a vertical layout: an embedded LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt:: at the top, a stretching horizontal layout below containing a LINK::Classes/ScrollView:: (timeline plus note canvas) and a fixed LINK::Classes/PianoRollSidebar:: on the right, and a transport strip along the bottom. That strip holds Start recording. Play loop and the Sync to menu (values 1 to 16, default 4) are shown only when the roll is not recording and contains at least one note. The sidebar shows the loop length from LINK::Classes/PianoRollLoopMarkers:: once both loop markers have been set, and, when exactly one note is selected, that note's CODE::midinote::, CODE::amp::, CODE::part:: (from LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote#-partNumber::), and any non-timing keys stored on its event. It embeds LINK::Classes/PianoRollTimeline:: for the beat strip above the roll (left/right clicks set loop bounds; Shift+left sets playback; see LINK::Classes/PianoRollTimeline::). LINK::#-receiveRecordingMidi:: draws LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote:: entries as LINK::Classes/BorderView:: regions from note-on and note-off messages. Part 1 uses LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour1::, part 2 uses LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour2::, part 3 uses LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour3::, and part 4 uses LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour4::. An unselected note's border is that colour at full opacity. A selected note's border is LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-extreme2::. The fill is the same colour at an opacity equal to the note's amplitude. Until CODE::\amp:: is written, that amplitude is the MIDI velocity mapped from 0–127 onto 0–1. LINK::Classes/AmpCommand:: sets CODE::\amp:: and the fill opacity follows it. LINK::#-startRecording:: and LINK::#-stopRecording:: announce CODE::\isRecording:: to dependants. LINK::#-stopRecording:: announces CODE::false:: before it finalizes the take, then updates LINK::Classes/PianoRollLoopMarkers:: from recorded notes. Keystrokes on the note area are reported to the LINK::Classes/SequencerKeyRouter:: passed in at construction.

SUBSECTION:: Keyboard editing
Focus the note area after clicking it:

TABLE::
## Keys || Behaviour
## 1–4 || Assign part on selected notes
## Escape || Focus the command prompt
::

Edits update the embedded LINK::Classes/SequencePlayer:: sequence and are allowed during playback. LINK::#-startRecording:: starts the LINK::Classes/Metronome::; LINK::#-stopRecording:: stops it. Note operations such as amp, delete, left, legato, right, snap, transpose, and write are invoked through the embedded LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt::. The prompt is constructed with LINK::Classes/AmpCommand#*new::, LINK::Classes/DeleteCommand#*new::, LINK::Classes/LeftCommand#*new::, LINK::Classes/LegatoCommand#*new::, LINK::Classes/RightCommand#*new::, LINK::Classes/SnapCommand#*new::, LINK::Classes/TransposeCommand#*new::, and LINK::Classes/WriteCommand#*new:: (passing the optional LINK::Classes/SequencerDocument::). Ambient parameters supply CODE::selectedNotes::, CODE::allNotes::, CODE::loopStart::, CODE::loopEnd::, and CODE::midiChannel::. CODE::loopStart:: and CODE::loopEnd:: are nil until both loop markers have been set. The CODE::delete:: command removes every selected note from the roll and from the sequence. The CODE::left:: and CODE::right:: commands move every selected note by the typed CODE::resolution::. The CODE::transpose:: command adds the typed integer to every selected note's MIDI note number. The CODE::write:: command inserts a CODE::~seq.addMidiSequence:: line via LINK::Classes/SequencerDocument#-insertPattern::.

SUBSECTION:: Navigation
The mouse wheel scrolls the roll vertically. Shift and the mouse wheel scroll it horizontally; wheel-up moves toward earlier beats. Ctrl and the mouse wheel zoom horizontally through four steps: half, the default scale, double, and quadruple. Wheel-up zooms in. The beat under the pointer stays put. Dragging a note moves its start time in steps of a quarter beat and its MIDI number by whole steps. The note view jumps to those positions while the button is held. A note that did not start on a quarter snaps to the nearest one once the pointer has moved. Dragging on empty roll space draws a rectangle and selects the notes inside it. Clicking a note selects that note. Without Ctrl, a click or an empty-space drag clears the previous selection first. Ctrl+drag on empty space and Ctrl+click add to the selection. Ctrl+click does not move the note. Clicking empty space clears the selection unless Ctrl is held.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a LINK::Classes/PianoRoll::.

ARGUMENT:: parent
Unused in the current implementation; reserved for embedding.

ARGUMENT:: bounds
Unused in the current implementation; reserved for layout.

ARGUMENT:: palette
A LINK::Classes/GuiPalette:: used for colours.

ARGUMENT:: sequencer
The LINK::Classes/Sequencer:: whose shared playback clock this roll uses for playback and recording.

ARGUMENT:: devMode
When true, skips MIDI setup and fills fake notes for development.

ARGUMENT:: keyRouter
The LINK::Classes/SequencerKeyRouter:: used for Record-view keyboard shortcuts.

ARGUMENT:: sequencerDocument
An optional LINK::Classes/SequencerDocument:: used to write pattern source. Pass CODE::nil:: when embedding without a document.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: commandPrompt
The embedded LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt:: instance used for command input.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt::.

METHOD:: focusBackground
Gives keyboard focus to the note area.

METHOD:: playLoop
Starts playback of the recorded sequence. The player acquires the sequencer's shared clock. When this play creates the clock, that clock is set to beat 0 first. The playhead then snaps to the nearest point on the LINK::#-syncTo:: grid that shares the clock's offset into that grid, measured from the loop start around the loop, and playback starts from there immediately. Returns false and posts a warning if no notes have been recorded.

METHOD:: assignSelectedToPart
Sets the part of every selected note. CODE::partNumber:: is an integer from 1 to 4.

ARGUMENT:: partNumber
The part to assign. An integer from 1 to 4.

METHOD:: selectedNotes
Returns an LINK::Classes/Array:: of currently selected LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote:: instances.

RETURNS::
An LINK::Classes/Array:: of LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote:: instances.

METHOD:: syncTo
The Sync-to grid in beats. An integer from 1 to 16. The default is 4. LINK::#-playLoop:: uses it to choose where the playhead starts.

ARGUMENT:: newSyncTo
The new grid size when setting. An integer from 1 to 16.

METHOD:: receiveRecordingMidi
Records one MIDI message into the open take. A note-on adds a LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote::. A note-off ends the open note of that number. Does nothing when this roll is not recording.

ARGUMENT:: msgType
CODE::\noteOn:: or CODE::\noteOff::.

ARGUMENT:: velocity
The note-on velocity.

ARGUMENT:: noteNumber
The MIDI note number.

ARGUMENT:: chan
The MIDI channel. A note-on stores it on the embedded LINK::Classes/SequencePlayer::.

METHOD:: startRecording
Acquires the sequencer's shared clock, creating it at beat 0 when nothing else holds it, and timestamps notes from that clock. In dev mode, fills fake notes. Starts the LINK::Classes/Metronome:: on that same clock, then announces CODE::\isRecording:: as CODE::true:: to dependants. Does nothing if recording is already in progress.

METHOD:: stopLoop
Stops playback via the embedded LINK::Classes/SequencePlayer:: and, after the final slice sends note-offs, releases that player's hold on the shared clock. Does nothing when playback is not in progress.

METHOD:: stopRecording
Announces CODE::\isRecording:: as CODE::false:: to dependants, stops the LINK::Classes/Metronome::, updates LINK::Classes/PianoRollLoopMarkers:: from recorded notes (loop bounds plus LINK::Classes/PianoRollLoopMarkers#-playheadTime_:: at the loop start beat), and releases this roll's hold on the shared clock. Does nothing when recording is not in progress.

PRIVATE:: init, prApplyNoteEdits, prAssignPartIfSelected, prColourForPart, prDeleteNote, prFillForNote, prPaintNote, prRefreshSidebar, prSelectedNotes, prUpdateLoopControls, prMakeTransportStrip
